 34CL c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), Sept 22, 2014                         
 34CL c  {+33}S+1p|){+34}Cl from J|p=3/2+ {+33}S ground state.                  
 34CL c  E({+3}He)=25 MeV. Measured deuteron spectra using Q3D magnetic         
 34CL2c  spectrograph at Munich. Several targets were used, all deposited on    
 34CL3c  7 |mg/cm{+2} 99.99% enriched {+12}C foils: 20 |mg/cm{+2} thick         
 34CL4c  99.9% enriched in {+33}S Ag{-2}{+33}S, 20 |mg/cm{+2} thick             
 34CL5c  natural sulphur Ag{-2}S, 50 |mg/cm{+2} thick Ag foil, 20 |mg/cm{+2}    
 34CL6c  thick 99.92% enriched {+24}Mg. Angular distributions were measured     
 34CL7c  from 10|' to 55|' in steps of 5|'. FWHM |? 12 keV. DWBA analysis of    
 34CL8c  |s(|q) data. Deduced levels, L-transfers, J, |p, spectroscopic         
 34CL9c  factors, resonance strengths and thermonuclear reaction rates for      
 34CLAc  {+33}S(p,|g){+34}Cl reaction, partial proton widths, {+32}S/{+33}S     
 34CLBc  ratio                                                                  
